Description: tolerate missing contrib LICENSE files under nodoc profile
 git's `debian/rules` `override_dh_installdocs-arch` target does a
 sanity-check `diff -q` between two contrib LICENSE files and the
 system common-licenses they'll later be symlinked to (via
 `debian/git.links`):
 .
   diff -q  …/contrib/persistent-https/LICENSE  /usr/share/common-licenses/Apache-2.0
   diff -bq …/contrib/subtree/COPYING          /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-2
 .
 The check confirms the bytes match before dh_link replaces the file
 with a symlink — protects against silent license-text drift when the
 git source ships a new revision of either LICENSE that no longer
 matches the common-licenses package.
 .
 Under `DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc` (Athena's default — `[Source]
 BuildProfiles = nodoc, nocheck` in build.conf), dh_installdocs is a
 partial no-op: it skips installing the contrib/* doc tree, so neither
 LICENSE file lands at the path the diff checks.  The diff then fails
 with "No such file or directory", returning rc=2, and
 dpkg-buildpackage aborts the binary stage with:
 .
   diff: …/usr/share/doc/git/contrib/persistent-https/LICENSE: No such file or directory
   make[1]: *** [debian/rules:151: override_dh_installdocs-arch] Error 2
 .
 Gate each diff on the source file existing.  When `nodoc` skipped the
 install, the diff is a no-op — dh_link's symlink target won't be
 there either, which is the expected `nodoc` shape (the
 contrib/persistent-https and contrib/subtree doc paths simply don't
 ship in the resulting .deb).  When `nodoc` is NOT in profiles, the
 files exist and the diff runs unchanged.
 .
 Captured during Athena's GROUPS-01 phase-3 gnome build on
 2026-05-14, where git is pulled in transitively by the
 [development-tools] group seed `build-essential` plus the [gnome]
 closure (gnome-shell → gjs → gobject-introspection → … → git).
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-14
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/rules
+++ b/debian/rules
@@ -148,8 +148,15 @@
 override_dh_installdocs-arch:
 	dh_installdocs --arch -X.gitignore
 	# These licenses are replaced with symlinks in git.links.
-	diff -q '$(GIT)'/usr/share/doc/git/contrib/persistent-https/LICENSE /usr/share/common-licenses/Apache-2.0
-	diff -bq '$(GIT)'/usr/share/doc/git/contrib/subtree/COPYING /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-2
+	# Gated on file existence: the `nodoc` build profile skips
+	# dh_installdocs's contrib/* copy, so the LICENSE files aren't
+	# installed in that mode and the diff would fail-stop the build.
+	# When absent, dh_link's symlink target won't exist either —
+	# that's the expected nodoc shape.
+	test ! -f '$(GIT)'/usr/share/doc/git/contrib/persistent-https/LICENSE || \
+	  diff -q '$(GIT)'/usr/share/doc/git/contrib/persistent-https/LICENSE /usr/share/common-licenses/Apache-2.0
+	test ! -f '$(GIT)'/usr/share/doc/git/contrib/subtree/COPYING || \
+	  diff -bq '$(GIT)'/usr/share/doc/git/contrib/subtree/COPYING /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-2
 	rm -rf '$(GIT)'/usr/share/doc/git/contrib/completion
 	rm -rf '$(GIT)'/usr/share/doc/git/contrib/emacs
 	rm -rf '$(GIT)'/usr/share/doc/git/contrib/hooks
